1
00:00:08,736 --> 00:00:14,786
This film is for teachers, faculty members and education researchers.

2
00:00:14,846 --> 00:00:22,063
It shows how a KuARK game gets harder, and why every difficulty is there.

3
00:00:22,773 --> 00:00:25,893
Every level runs the same loop.

4
00:00:25,953 --> 00:00:31,073
Predict what will happen, change one setting and test it.

5
00:00:31,133 --> 00:00:36,413
The board redraws the science from the level’s own numbers.

6
00:00:36,473 --> 00:00:42,402
Then explain why it worked, and carry the idea to a new case.

7
00:00:43,312 --> 00:00:47,432
Every game has twenty levels in five stages.

8
00:00:47,492 --> 00:00:54,605
Each stage adds one kind of challenge, so learners always know what is new.

9
00:00:55,315 --> 00:00:58,255
Levels 1 to 3: one setting.

10
00:00:58,315 --> 00:01:05,055
One cause, one effect; everything else stays still, so a first model can form.

11
00:01:05,115 --> 00:01:12,910
Even here the projectile has two correct angles: a model can have more than one answer.

12
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:16,820
Levels 4 to 6: a fixed variable.

13
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:21,000
Now the angle is held and the speed changes.

14
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:29,182
This is the control of variables: change one thing and keep the rest.

15
00:01:29,892 --> 00:01:33,172
Levels 7 to 10: combine settings.

16
00:01:33,232 --> 00:01:39,202
Angle and speed are chosen together, and a limit appears: a ceiling.

17
00:01:39,262 --> 00:01:47,487
Learners weigh trade-offs and find that several combinations can work.

18
00:01:48,197 --> 00:01:51,137
Levels 11 to 15: expert.

19
00:01:51,197 --> 00:01:57,247
A genuinely new idea enters: a wall, a second medium, another planet.

20
00:01:57,307 --> 00:02:05,792
The model is extended rather than replaced; that is what transfer looks like.

21
00:02:06,502 --> 00:02:09,622
Levels 16 to 20: master design.

22
00:02:09,682 --> 00:02:16,042
Several limits must hold at once: a height, a ridge, a different gravity.

23
00:02:16,102 --> 00:02:24,097
The task becomes design under constraints, as in real engineering and research.

24
00:02:24,807 --> 00:02:31,857
A setting that only the later levels use stays fixed and hidden in levels 1 to 10.

25
00:02:31,917 --> 00:02:40,368
It appears when the new idea needs it, so the early levels stay simple.

26
00:02:41,078 --> 00:02:44,898
Some difficulties are placed on purpose.

27
00:02:44,958 --> 00:02:52,008
The answer appears only after the level is solved, so learners have to produce it.

28
00:02:52,068 --> 00:02:58,038
They predict first, and feedback shows the direction, not the value.

29
00:02:58,098 --> 00:03:03,838
Hints come in three tiers: strategy, formula, then the full path.

30
00:03:03,898 --> 00:03:12,910
Stars reward method: at least two tries in different conditions, then the reasoning task.

31
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:21,510
In learning-science terms, the stages move from a low-load start to the control of variables,

32
00:03:21,570 --> 00:03:29,160
then to covariation and trade-offs, to transfer, and finally to design under constraints.

33
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:35,283
The difficulty grows in the reasoning, not only in the numbers.

34
00:03:35,993 --> 00:03:45,043
Under the hood, each scenario comes from a seed and is checked for at least one solution before it is shown.

35
00:03:45,103 --> 00:03:53,693
When a signed-in learner solves a level, the server replays it with the same seed and the same engine.

36
00:03:53,753 --> 00:04:01,033
The same seed always gives the same scenario, so a lesson or a study can be repeated.

37
00:04:01,093 --> 00:04:11,893
In formula games the accepted band tightens in four steps, and a link can open exactly the levels a lesson needs.

38
00:04:12,603 --> 00:04:15,803
The design itself can be tested.

39
00:04:15,863 --> 00:04:26,833
With consent and ethics approval, the platform randomises choices such as the prediction step, the feedback style and the hint tiers.

40
00:04:26,893 --> 00:04:37,173
An honest limit: passing level 20 alone does not certify proficiency; that needs pilots and independent pre- and post-tests.

41
00:04:37,233 --> 00:04:42,402
If you study learning, we would like to work with you.

